MLLM description: The Arctic fox is a small, stocky mammal with a thick, dense fur coat that provides excellent insulation against the cold. Its distinctive physical features include a rounded head, large ears, and a short tail. The fur coloration varies depending on the season; in summer, it is typically grayish-brown, while in winter, it turns white to blend into the snowy environment.

Behaviorally, Arctic foxes are known for their agility and adaptability. They are skilled hunters, often preying on small rodents like lemmings and voles, and can also scavenge for food. Their keen sense of smell and hearing allows them to locate prey even under snow cover. Arctic foxes are also social animals, living in family groups called "sets" that consist of an adult pair and their offspring.

